= Levi's Letter

The strike in Central Germany was lost, but it was not a putsch, and Levi knows it. He writes a long letter to Lenin, not a pamphlet. The strike was right, he says, and badly prepared: the party asked the workers to fight before it had won them. He asks for one thing, that the International stop sending emissaries who decide German questions in hotel rooms.

[? if e21_levi_resigned = 1 : Levi has been out of the Zentrale since February. His friends say it is time he came back. ?][? if e21_levi_resigned = 0 : Levi still holds the chair. The Left says the defeat is his, since he would not let the party fight properly. ?]

- @return: Bring Levi back to the head of the party.
- @counsel: Keep the present leadership, and listen to him.
- @sideline: Sideline him: the defeat proves the Left right.

@return
subtitle: The Spartacist line. The Left will not take it quietly.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
Q.leading_faction = 'luxemburgist';
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.e21_levi_resigned = 0;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 12;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 12;
Q.independence += 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
!}

The Central Committee asks Levi and Zetkin to return. Levi takes the chair again, on condition that the emissaries are recalled. Kun leaves Berlin in a temper.

@counsel
subtitle: The Right's way: Brandler leads, Levi advises. Nobody is quite satisfied.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
if (Q.leading_faction == 'offensive') {
    Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
    Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
}
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 8;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The Zentrale keeps its leaders but changes its tone. The theory of the offensive is quietly dropped from the Rote Fahne, and Levi's letter is circulated to the Central Committee.

@sideline
subtitle: The Left's line. Levi is pushed to the edge of the party.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 10;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 12;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist -= 1;
!}

The Zentrale resolves that the strike failed because it was not bold enough. Levi is removed from every committee he still sits on. His case, his friends say, will go to Moscow.
